    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP on August 15 is headlined by **Corbin Carroll**, who sits at an elite 82.38 score against Grant Holmes. Despite the minor concern regarding Holmes's ability to control the run game, **Corbin Carroll** remains our top priority due to his unparalleled ability to steal bases\u2014a category we treat as gold in this league\u2014coupled with a favorable matchup against a 4.65 xERA arm. Joining him in the elite tier are **Josh Naylor** (72.72) and **Seiya Suzuki** (68.78). **Josh Naylor** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Hayden Wesneski, whose high xERA (4.92) gives our heart-of-the-order slugger massive RBI potential, while **Seiya Suzuki** exploits a high-floor matchup against McGreevy to maintain his status as a locked-in starter.\n\nOur platoon-heavy approach today is anchored by **Mickey Moniak**, whose score of 63.36 is bolstered significantly by a +14% boost from a favorable right-handed platoon matchup, and **Brice Turang** (66.26), who gains additional value from a wind-aided atmosphere and a slow delivery from Justin Wrobleski that effectively creates a green light for his speed profile. We are closely monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes**; while **Gabriel Moreno** maintains a strong 67.77 score, the lack of an official lineup means we are relying on an assumed #3 spot. **Isaac Paredes** faces a tighter path to value against Emerson Hancock; his 55.07 score sits at the lower end of our active spectrum, but he remains in the lineup to capitalize on his own dynamic platoon advantage.\n\nThe toughest decision of the morning was the benching of **Travis Bazzana**. With a respectable score of 46.43, he was the final cut from our utility considerations, ultimately passed over because our current configuration favors the higher situational upside provided by **Austin Riley** and **Max Muncy**. While **Travis Bazzana** is ready to contribute, our priority remains the high-efficiency scoring spots. We continue to hold **Jose Caballero**, **James Wood**, and **Trevor Story** on the bench due to their inactive or injured status; we are eagerly anticipating the return of **James Wood** to inject high-ceiling production back into our outfield rotation once his IL stint concludes.",
